<section class="page-hero"><img class="bg" src="/assets/img/photos/hero-home-after-rain.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hero-home-after-rain-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hero-home-after-rain.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.12"><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/cities-we-serve/">Cities we serve</a><span>/</span>Santa Fe</nav><span class="kicker light fade-up">Northern Mountains &amp; Four Corners</span><h1 class="fade-up" style="animation-delay:.06s">Insurance Appraiser in Santa Fe, New Mexico</h1><p class="lede fade-up" style="animation-delay:.14s">In Santa Fe the cost of a repair often depends on rules as much as materials. We appraise losses on adobe, Pueblo Revival and Territorial homes where historic-district requirements, flat roofs and high-elevation winters all shape the number.</p><div class="btn-row fade-up" style="animation-delay:.22s;margin-top:26px"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn light" href="/contact-new-mexico-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><div class="facts fade-up" style="animation-delay:.3s"><div><small>County</small><b>Santa Fe County</b></div><div><small>Region</small><b>Northern Mountains &amp; Four Corners</b></div><div><small>Housing</small><b>Pueblo Revival and Territorial homes, historic adobe, flat parapet roofs, pitched metal roofs in the foothills</b></div></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="note"><b class="h">Claim risks around Santa Fe</b><ul class="chips-row"><li>Snow and ice on flat roofs</li><li>Freeze-burst pipes</li><li>Hail</li><li>Canale and parapet leaks</li><li>Wildfire smoke</li></ul></div>

<h2>High desert, high elevation, high standards</h2>
<p>Santa Fe sits at roughly 7,000 feet at the foot of the Sangre de Cristo Mountains, and that elevation defines its claims. Winters bring snow that lingers on flat roofs, freeze-thaw cycles that open parapet joints, and cold snaps that burst pipes in exterior walls. Summer monsoon storms can deliver hail and heavy rain that overwhelms canales and scuppers. In recent years, wildfire smoke from fires across northern New Mexico has also become a recurring source of interior cleaning and contents claims.</p>
<h2>The Historic Styles rules and why they matter</h2>
<p>Within Santa Fe’s historic districts, exterior work is reviewed under the city’s historic design standards, which call for Old Santa Fe Style, meaning Pueblo Revival or Territorial, along with specific requirements for materials, colors, window types and parapet details. The Historic Districts Review Board and city preservation staff oversee those rules. When a storm or fire damages a home on <strong>Canyon Road</strong>, on the <strong>Eastside</strong> or near the Plaza, the repair has to satisfy those standards, and that can mean more labor, specialty plaster, true divided-light windows or hand-formed details that an off-the-shelf estimate omits.</p>
<p>Whether a policy pays for the added cost of complying with ordinances often depends on its ordinance or law coverage. That’s a policy question worth reading closely. The pricing of the compliant repair itself is something appraisal can address.</p>
<h2>Across the city and county</h2>
<p>Historic adobe homes with mud plaster or lime finishes need different methods from the cement stucco common in newer construction. Outside the historic core, much of Santa Fe’s housing is frame-and-stucco Pueblo-style homes with flat built-up or modified bitumen roofs behind parapets. South of town, <strong>Eldorado</strong> mixes passive-solar designs, flat roofs and pitched metal on large lots exposed to wind. North of the city, <strong>Tesuque</strong> includes estate properties with long driveways, outbuildings, older adobe and extensive landscaping, all of which complicate scope.</p>
<h2>Disputes we see in Santa Fe</h2>
<ul>
<li>Flat-roof leaks after snow and ice, written as maintenance rather than sudden damage.</li>
<li>Adobe walls and mud plaster priced as standard cement stucco.</li>
<li>Historic-district requirements for windows, doors and parapet caps left out of the scope.</li>
<li>Vigas, latillas and corbels damaged by water or smoke where replacement wood and craftsmanship are underpriced.</li>
<li>Smoke-affected contents and HVAC systems after regional wildfires.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/appraiser-services/flat-roof-stucco-appraisal/">flat roof and stucco appraisal</a>, <a href="/appraiser-services/winter-freeze-damage-appraisal/">winter freeze appraisal</a> and <a href="/appraiser-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">fire and smoke appraisal</a> pages explain each issue.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Document before you repair</b>On a historic property, take photos of every damaged detail, keep samples of original plaster or trim where you safely can, and save any correspondence with city preservation staff. Those records make it far easier to price a faithful repair.</div>
<h2>How we help</h2>
<p>We serve Santa Fe from our statewide practice without a local office. We read your policy, inspect the home with its construction and any review requirements in mind, and prepare a scope that reflects how the repair must actually be done. If the difference is a matter of pricing, an <a href="/appraiser-services/claim-estimate-review/">estimate review</a> may be enough. If not, we can act as your appraiser or, where both parties agree, as an <a href="/appraiser-services/umpire-services/">umpire</a>. Neighbors in <a href="/cities-we-serve/los-alamos/">Los Alamos</a> face similar winter issues. <a href="/contact-new-mexico-appraiser/">Contact us</a> to begin.</p>

<h2>Services available in Santa Fe</h2>
<p>Every New Mexico Insurance Appraiser service is available in Santa Fe and the rest of Santa Fe County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/appraiser-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/hail-roof-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/high-wind-damage-appraisal/">High Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/wildfire-loss-appraisal/">Wildfire Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Santa Fe claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does my insurer have to pay for historic-district compliant repairs in Santa Fe?</summary><div class="a"><p>It depends on your policy, particularly any ordinance or law coverage and how it is worded. The cost of a compliant repair can be valued in appraisal, while questions about whether the policy covers it should go to a New Mexico attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal address damage to a true adobe wall?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Appraisal values the cost to repair the actual construction, so an adobe wall with mud or lime plaster should be priced with the materials and methods it requires, not as a cement stucco patch.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are wildfire smoke claims common in Santa Fe even without a nearby fire?</summary><div class="a"><p>They can be. Heavy smoke from fires elsewhere in northern New Mexico can affect interiors, HVAC systems and contents, and disagreements often center on how much cleaning or replacement is reasonable.</p></div></details></div>
